<title>CHILE: Chile's Iansa Q1 net off sharply.</title>
<headline>Chile's Iansa Q1 net off sharply.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean foodmaker Industria Azucarera Nacional SA, or Iansa, posted net first quarter profits of $4.6 million, off 39 percent from net profits in the same quarter of 1996, CEO Juan Obach said.</p>
<p>First quarter sales were 56 billion pesos, or $134 million, Obach said. Other results were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Obach attributed the drop to lower sugar production at the company's own plantations, forcing more imports, which cut profit margins.</p>
<p>-- Rodrigo Martinez/Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-6995595</p>
